# logs — runtime artifacts written by the local BTD/Litgrid fetch cron.
# logs/btd.log was tracked by accident (f551934); it churns on every run, which
# blocked a rebase and contributed to two stale deploys on 2026-07-29.
logs/

# doc artifacts (screenshots, traces — point-in-time verification, not reference)
docs/**/*.png
!docs/visual-audit/phase-*/
!docs/visual-audit/phase-*/*.png
!docs/visual-audit/phase-*/**/*.png
docs/**/*.json
!docs/audits/phase-*/*.json
# Phase 41 — the provenance graph is generated, and tracked ANYWAY, deliberately.
#
# C1 says generated files are never tracked, and the case it was written for is
# a log that blocked a rebase. This is the other kind: a small deterministic
# artifact whose committed copy IS the reference the reproducibility gate
# compares a fresh generation against. Untracked, `build-graph.mjs --check` has
# nothing to check in CI and the gate silently stops being one. Same pattern and
# same justification as the tracked `regression-baseline.json` and
# `eslint-baseline.json`.
!docs/provenance/graph.json
# Phase 49 — the C3 pre-state, tracked for the same reason as the graph above.
#
# C3 requires the pre-state of anything a phase intends to move to be captured
# FIRST, as its own artifact. C4 requires numbers to cross sessions via committed
# artifacts rather than conversational memory. An untracked pre-state satisfies
# neither: the delta table in the CP would be a claim with nothing behind it, and
# the next phase to touch these fields would have no baseline to subtract from.
# Deterministic (54 configs × one frozen KV snapshot), ~200 KB, regenerated by
# `scripts/_phase-49-prestate.mjs`.
!docs/investigations/*-prestate.json
# Same reasoning for the measured deltas a CP is signed against: a delta table in
# a handover with no artifact behind it is a claim, not a measurement.
!docs/investigations/*-delta.json
claude-handover/images/

